Un-premultiplies colors in Color::toArray as r / a * 255 instead of
r * 255 / a. The channels are floats, so r * 255 rounds before the division,
and a full channel with partial alpha comes back as 254.99998474121094:
'#ff000080' evaluates to ["rgba",254.99998474121094,0,0,0.5], and to-rgba,
serialize and stringify carry the same noise. Dividing first gives exactly 1
when r == a. GL JS also divides first: Color.rgb divides by alpha, then
to-rgba scales by 255.
Upstream: not proposed

diff --git a/src/mln/util/color.cpp b/src/mln/util/color.cpp
index 132336c..67e9f0c 100644
--- a/src/mln/util/color.cpp
+++ b/src/mln/util/color.cpp
@@ -196,9 +196,9 @@ std::array<double, 4> Color::toArray() const {
         return {{0, 0, 0, 0}};
     } else {
         return {{
-            r * 255 / a,
-            g * 255 / a,
-            b * 255 / a,
+            r / a * 255,
+            g / a * 255,
+            b / a * 255,
             floor(a * 100 + .5) / 100 // round to 2 decimal places
         }};
     }
